---
// [AUMFE-HELP-LEGAL-PREVIEW-1] ADMIN-ONLY preview of the PROPOSED new legal sections for the voice
// guides and the wallet. They are NOT on the public Terms / Privacy / Refunds pages and must not be
// copied there until a payment gateway is approved and the owner has settled the [CONFIRM WITH OWNER]
// items below.
//
// NOTE FOR AI:
//  - Server-rendered (prerender = false) behind the Admin 2 shell (client admin guard via
//    GET /api/admin/whoami; noindex). Nothing here is prerendered, so no static HTML under dist/
//    contains this text.
//  - Styles are the folk legal ones (styles/legal-folk.css, scoped under `.folk-site .lg`), the same
//    classes pages/terms.astro, privacy.astro and refunds.astro use.
//  - CLAUDE.md "THERE IS NO COMPANY": no entity is named or implied. Text says "we" and uses
//    BRAND.name only. Emails are plain text "name (@) domain", never mailto.
//  - Money: 1 token = ₹1 and Meera is ₹6 per started minute (owner decisions, 2026-10-02). Adding
//    money to the wallet is "coming soon" — there is no top-up yet.
//  - NOTE for whoever publishes: today's Refunds section 1 says "There are no tokens, wallets, credits
//    or extra charges added at checkout." That is about event checkout and stays true, but add
//    "This does not apply to voice calls, which are paid from your wallet" when "Wallet and tokens"
//    goes live, so the two do not read as a contradiction.
export const prerender = false;
import Admin2 from '../../../layouts/Admin2.astro';
import PreviewRibbon from '../../../components/PreviewRibbon.tsx';
import { BRAND } from '../../../lib/brand';
import '../../../styles/saathum-folk.css';
import '../../../styles/legal-folk.css';

const toc = [
  { id: 'terms-voice', label: 'Terms: Voice guides, AI and paid calls' },
  { id: 'terms-wallet', label: 'Terms and Refunds: Wallet and tokens' },
  { id: 'refunds-minutes', label: 'Refunds: Voice call minutes' },
  { id: 'privacy-voice', label: 'Privacy: Voice calls, recordings and memory' },
];
---

<Admin2
  title="Legal preview"
  heading="Legal preview: proposed new sections"
  subtitle="Hidden until a payment gateway is approved. These sections are not on the public Terms, Privacy or Refunds pages."
  active="preview-legal"
>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow" slot="head" />
  <div class="mb-5"><PreviewRibbon client:load force /></div>

  <div class="folk-site" data-design="reference-v5">
    <div class="lg pv-legal">
      <div class="lg-body-inner">
        <aside class="lg-rail">
          <nav class="lg-toc" aria-label="Proposed sections">
            <b>Proposed sections</b>
            <ol>
              {toc.map((item) => <li><a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.label}</a></li>)}
            </ol>
          </nav>
          <div class="lg-rail-card">
            <div>
              <b>Before this goes live</b>
              <span>Three items marked CONFIRM WITH OWNER need a decision. Nothing here is published.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <article class="lg-article"><div class="lg-prose">
          <p>
            These are the new sections we plan to add for voice guides and the wallet, shown in the
            same look as the live legal pages. Each one says which page it will be added to.
          </p>

          <!-- ============ TERMS: VOICE GUIDES ============ -->
          <div class="lg-note lg-note--plain">
            <div>
              <span class="lg-tag">Will be added to: Terms of Service</span>
              <p>New section, placed after the existing section on using the site.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 id="terms-voice"><span class="lg-n">NEW</span>Voice guides, AI and paid calls</h2>
          <p>
            {BRAND.name} offers guides you can talk to: Meera speaks with you by voice, Pandit ji
            chats with you in writing, and Preeti helps you around the site. All of them are
            <strong>AI</strong>. They are not people, and we will always tell you so.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Guidance only.</strong> A guide shares what Hindu tradition says about your
            question, to help you think it through. It does not promise any outcome, and nothing a
            guide says is a prediction you should rely on.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Not professional advice.</strong> A guide does not give medical, legal or
            financial advice. For those, please speak to a qualified professional. In an emergency,
            call your local emergency number.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Adults only.</strong> Voice guides are for people aged 18 or over.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>How minutes are charged.</strong> Voice calls with Meera are paid from your
            wallet at ₹6 (6 tokens) for every minute you start. A call that ends within 10 seconds is
            free. You need at least one minute's balance to begin a call. The price is shown before
            you start.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>When your balance runs out.</strong> The call ends politely. You are never
            charged for more than your wallet holds. Pandit ji and Preeti are free.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Fair use.</strong> Please use the guides in good faith. Do not use them to
            harass, to ask for anything unlawful, or to copy or resell what they say. We may limit or
            stop access if the service is being misused.
          </p>

          <!-- ============ TERMS + REFUNDS: WALLET ============ -->
          <div class="lg-note lg-note--plain">
            <div>
              <span class="lg-tag">Will be added to: Terms of Service and Refunds</span>
              <p>Same section in both places, or in Terms with a link from Refunds.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 id="terms-wallet"><span class="lg-n">NEW</span>Wallet and tokens</h2>
          <p>
            Your {BRAND.name} wallet holds <strong>tokens</strong>. <strong>1 token is worth ₹1.</strong>
            Tokens pay for voice calls. They are not money in a bank account, they earn no interest,
            and they can be used only on {BRAND.name}.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Not transferable.</strong> Tokens belong to your account. You cannot send them to
            another person or sell them.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Adding money.</strong> Adding money to the wallet is coming soon. Until then
            there is no top-up.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Credits from us.</strong> Sometimes our team adds tokens to your wallet, for
            example to put right a problem on our side. These show in your wallet like any other
            tokens. If a credit was made by mistake, we may take it back and we will tell you.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Refunds go back as tokens.</strong> When we refund a call, the tokens return to
            your wallet.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Unused balance.</strong> [CONFIRM WITH OWNER: what happens to unused tokens. Can
            they be refunded to the bank, do they expire, and what happens if an account is closed?]
          </p>

          <!-- ============ REFUNDS: VOICE CALL MINUTES ============ -->
          <div class="lg-note lg-note--plain">
            <div>
              <span class="lg-tag">Will be added to: Refunds &amp; Cancellations</span>
              <p>New section, after "Wrong or duplicate payments".</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 id="refunds-minutes"><span class="lg-n">NEW</span>Voice call minutes</h2>
          <p>
            Calls are charged for each <strong>started minute</strong>. If you speak for 2 minutes
            and 20 seconds, that is 3 minutes.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Under 10 seconds is free.</strong> If the call ends within 10 seconds, nothing is
            charged.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>If something goes wrong on our side.</strong> If a call fails because of a
            technical problem on our side, we credit the minutes back to your wallet as tokens.
            [CONFIRM WITH OWNER: the exact rule, for example whether it is automatic or on request,
            and the time limit to ask.]
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Minutes you used.</strong> A call that worked is not refunded because you did not
            like the guidance, or because the outcome was not what you hoped for. Guidance is not a
            guarantee.
          </p>
          <p>
            To ask about a call, write to support (@) {BRAND.domain} with the date and time and what
            happened.
          </p>

          <!-- ============ PRIVACY ============ -->
          <div class="lg-note lg-note--plain">
            <div>
              <span class="lg-tag">Will be added to: Privacy Policy</span>
              <p>New section, after the section on information we collect.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 id="privacy-voice"><span class="lg-n">NEW</span>Voice calls, recordings and memory</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>We keep text, not audio.</strong> We write down your calls and chats as text
            transcripts and store them privately. We do not keep an audio recording of your voice.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Who processes your voice.</strong> To run a call, AI services process your voice
            live, so they can hear you and speak back. We choose these services carefully and share
            only what is needed to run the call.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Summaries and remembered facts.</strong> If you allow it, we also keep short
            summaries of your talks and a few facts about you, such as your birth details and what you
            asked about, so your guides do not make you repeat yourself. Pandit ji, Preeti and Meera
            share this one memory. If you do not allow it, they do not remember.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>You are in control.</strong> You can see what is remembered, delete any single
            item, or tell a guide to "forget me" and everything is erased.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>How long we keep it.</strong> Transcripts and memories are kept for up to 12
            months, then deleted. Our staff open a transcript only for support or safety, and we never
            sell your talks.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Palm photos.</strong> If you use a guide that reads your palm with your camera,
            the photo is used for your reading. [CONFIRM WITH OWNER: whether the photo is kept, for how
            long, and who can see it.]
          </p>
        </div></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Admin2>

<style is:global>
  .pv-legal .lg-body-inner { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 280px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 32px; align-items: start; }
  .pv-legal .lg-rail { position: sticky; top: 16px; }
  .pv-legal .lg-note { margin-top: 36px; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .pv-legal .lg-body-inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .pv-legal .lg-rail { position: static; }
  }
</style>
